meta {
  name: Create Daily Log - Medication
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/{{houseId}}/young-persons/{{youngPersonId}}/daily-logs
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  chronology_id: 8
  activity_action: Administered morning medication as prescribed. Medication: Fluoxetine 20mg (1 capsule). Taken with breakfast. YP cooperative, no issues with administration. No adverse reactions noted. Next dose due tomorrow.
  mood[0]: Calm
  breakfast: Toast and orange juice (taken with medication)
  ~attachments[0]: @file(/path/to/medication_record.pdf)
}

docs {
  # Create Daily Log - Medication
  
  Record medication administration and related observations.
  
  ## Required Fields
  - `chronology_id` (integer): Must be 8 (Medication)
  
  **Note:** `date`, `log_date_time`, and `day_part` are automatically set by the server.
  - `activity_action` (string, required): Detailed medication record
  
  ## Critical Information to Include
  
  ### Medication Details
  - **Medication name** (generic and brand if applicable)
  - **Dosage** (exact amount)
  - **Route** (oral, topical, inhaler, etc.)
  - **Time administered** (exact time)
  - **Administered by** (staff member name)
  
  ### Administration
  - Whether taken as prescribed
  - Any difficulties in administration
  - Taken with food/water
  - YP cooperation level
  
  ### Observations
  - Any immediate reactions
  - Effectiveness of medication
  - Side effects noted
  - YP's mood/behaviour after taking
  
  ### Next Steps
  - Next dose due date/time
  - Any follow-up required
  - Medication reviews scheduled
  
  ## Optional Fields
  - `day_part` (string): Auto-detected (usually Morning/Evening for regular meds)
  - `mood` (array): YP's mood at time of administration
  - `breakfast`, `lunch`, `dinner`: Meal taken with medication
  - `attachments` (files): Medication charts, prescription copies
  
  ## Example Entries
  
  ### Regular Medication
  ```
  Morning dose administered at 08:00.
  Medication: Methylphenidate 18mg (1 tablet)
  Route: Oral
  Taken with: Breakfast and water
  YP cooperation: Fully cooperative
  Observations: No adverse reactions. YP reports feeling focused.
  Administered by: Sarah Johnson (Staff)
  Next dose: 08:00 tomorrow
  ```
  
  ### PRN (As Needed) Medication
  ```
  PRN medication given at 14:30.
  Medication: Paracetamol 500mg (2 tablets)
  Reason: YP complained of headache (pain level 6/10)
  Route: Oral with water
  Parent permission: Obtained via phone
  Observations: Pain reduced to 3/10 after 30 minutes. 
  YP rested quietly. No adverse reactions.
  Can repeat in 4 hours if needed.
  Administered by: Mark Thompson (Staff)
  ```
  
  ### Refused Medication
  ```
  Medication offered at 20:00 as prescribed.
  Medication: Melatonin 2mg
  Status: REFUSED
  Reason given: YP stated "not tired, want to finish game"
  Actions: Explained importance of sleep routine. Offered again 
  20 minutes later - YP accepted second offer.
  Time taken: 20:20
  Observations: YP settled for bed by 21:00. Normal sleep pattern.
  Administered by: Emma Davies (Staff)
  ```
  
  ### Medication Error
  ```
  Medication error identified at 12:30.
  Issue: Morning dose (08:00) was not administered due to staff 
  handover miscommunication.
  Action taken: Senior staff notified immediately. Parent/guardian 
  contacted. Dose administered at 12:45 with medical approval.
  Incident report: Completed (Ref: IR-2026-001)
  Follow-up: Review handover procedures. No adverse effects on YP.
  ```
  
  ## Safety Guidelines
  - Double-check medication against prescription
  - Verify young person identity
  - Document immediately after administration
  - Never leave medication unattended
  - Report any concerns to medical staff
  - Maintain secure medication storage
  
  ## Response (201 Created)
  Returns the created medication log with all safety checks documented.
}
